### Footnotes

<sup id="footnote-1">1</sup> - Flights are counted by take-off, so flights that are divided with technical/transit stop, like when a flight from Sydney to London stops in Singapore for about 40 min, are counted as two flights.

<sup id="footnote-2">2</sup> - The number of known individual airframes flown, counted by number of different tail numbers. This number is an under count because there are some flights with unknown tail numbers.

<sup id="footnote-3">3</sup> - Number of flights which the tail number for an aircraft is unknown.

<sup id="footnote-4">4</sup> - Some of the flights don't have the actual flight time, just the estimated flight time, so consider this an estimate.

